course: dictionary
lesson: 9789
title: Survive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To survive means to stay alive, especially through something dangerous. It can also mean to last through something hard and still be there. «The old church survived the storm.» The church was not knocked down, so it survived.
explain: Look at the words around survive for clues. «Walking sharks can survive for hours with very little oxygen when a rock pool gets warm and stale at low tide.» Hours with very little oxygen is dangerous, so survive means keep living through it.
explain: Survive can also mean to live longer than someone. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Survive» is a verb: survive, survives, survived, surviving.
fact: «Survive» means to stay alive, especially through something dangerous.
fact: «Survive» can also mean to last through something hard and still be there.
fact: Survivors are the ones left after some have died or been lost: survivors = total − lost.
fact: Living things need food, water, air and shelter to survive, and animals can adapt to survive.
exercise: «Walking sharks can survive for hours with very little oxygen.» What does survive mean here? | To sleep in a cave | *To stay alive | To swim very fast | To change colour
exercise: Of 20 seeds planted, 6 did not grow. How many survived? | 6 | *14 | 20 | 26
exercise: «The old church survived the storm.» Which phrase means the same as survived here? | *Lasted through the storm and was still there | Was painted green | Ran away | Fell down
test: «Darwin's finches with beaks that fitted the food survived better.» What does survived better mean? | Changed their songs | *Stayed alive and had a better chance | Lost their beaks | Flew much faster
test: What does it mean to survive someone? | *To live longer than them | To forget them | To hug them | To shout at them
exam: Which sentence uses survive to mean stay alive through danger? | I survive my homework | *The sailors survived the shipwreck | The sun will survive at noon | We survive on toast every day
